# Written by a running instance's startup command, not by any build step. That
# command writes it with a RELATIVE path, so the file lands wherever the
# container's working directory happens to point -- an older layout put one at
# the repository root, where it went stale and was later read as though it were
# current. Anchored to the single path the current layout writes, so a copy
# anywhere else shows up as untracked rather than being hidden. This does not
# stop a stray one being written; it stops one being invisible.
/apps/opencroft/.deploy-marker
